## Test that llvm-bolt correctly skips functions with exception handlers.
## Functions flagged with UNW_FLAG_EHANDLER or UNW_FLAG_UHANDLER have opaque
## handler data that contains embedded code offsets. Rewriting these functions
## would corrupt the handler data, so BOLT must skip them.

# RUN: yaml2obj %p/Inputs/exception-handler.yaml -o %t.exe
# RUN: llvm-bolt %t.exe -o %t.out.exe 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: processing PE/COFF binary
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: parsed 3 .pdata entries
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: 3 functions discovered from .pdata
# CHECK: BOLT-INFO: 1 functions with exception handlers (skipped)
